The brief combines a sales bar chart with an on-call incident panel. Charts and ops both fit, but I have to pick one. The bar chart is the main visual element, and the incident panel (status, notifications) is smaller. The ops catalogue also covers dashboards, incidents and on-call work, which is arguably the broader fit. The charts catalogue covers only the chart. The standard catalogue is always resolved, so it may already supply basic bar charts, but the charts catalogue is dedicated to them.

I'm choosing ops, since it covers the dashboard framing and the on-call incident panel, and a simple bar chart is the lesser need.

